                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "669e468f-39ec-3ef8-8604-c0ca90db5efa",
                        "entry_id": "4e5fcabd-a39b-385b-b934-e26bdca68327",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ausgelassenes, fröhliches, meist lautes Treiben, beispielsweise auf einer Party"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "04723e41-f600-46ed-8393-6cc272129aa8",
                                "sense_id": "669e468f-39ec-3ef8-8604-c0ca90db5efa",
                                "text": "Die Teilnehmer des Faschings machten eine Menge Halligalli."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7354eef9-0c7b-438c-b75e-170f26a8cc83",
                                "sense_id": "669e468f-39ec-3ef8-8604-c0ca90db5efa",
                                "text": "[…] die beiden Extrem-Entertainer Joko und Klaas [machen] jede Menge Halligalli im Fernsehen und lassen keine noch so alberne Idee ungenutzt, wenn dabei nur ein vor Schadenfreude triefender Gag herausspringt."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "13eec786-b6b5-4b1d-8dc1-13b936b9278f",
                                "sense_id": "669e468f-39ec-3ef8-8604-c0ca90db5efa",
                                "text": "„[…] es gibt auch Menschen, die nicht nur Halligalli auf dem [Kreuzfahrt-]Schiff wollen, sondern die auch Tiefergehendes möchten, Spirituelles suchen oder die es gewohnt sind, in ihrer Heimatstadt zum Gottesdienst zur Kirche zu gehen […].“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d7e71948-fd75-40d7-b58e-8e27899a9f94",
                                "sense_id": "669e468f-39ec-3ef8-8604-c0ca90db5efa",
                                "text": "Jahrelang habe ich mit Depressionen zu kämpfen gehabt. […] Anfangs probierte ich, meine Ängste mit einem Leben voll Halligalli, Therapien, Kiffen und mit zwei Selbstmordversuchen in den Griff zu kriegen."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7ae20b3d-e238-32d4-9a13-e2daf1b3cb68",
                        "entry_id": "4e5fcabd-a39b-385b-b934-e26bdca68327",
                        "glosses": [
                            "unerwünschter Lärm, unerwünschter Trubel"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea9c50af-843b-4e68-abe4-ade3d35d3e06",
                                "sense_id": "7ae20b3d-e238-32d4-9a13-e2daf1b3cb68",
                                "text": "[Mama zum Kind:] „Jetzt mach' kein Halligalli und geh' ins Bett!“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "25a95da2-722a-4f0e-a814-1ee09bb8aee2",
                                "sense_id": "7ae20b3d-e238-32d4-9a13-e2daf1b3cb68",
                                "text": "Die [hannoveraner Notübernachtung in der] Celler Straße war berühmt, dass es dort immer Halligalli gab, es war immer Stress da, also immer auch mal Schlägereien, alles."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "732ba997-3d17-41da-bf3e-5c8635cce125",
                                "sense_id": "7ae20b3d-e238-32d4-9a13-e2daf1b3cb68",
                                "text": "Ein Auto dröhnt vorbei, sie [Museumschefin Alexandra Hildebrandt] unterbricht. „Hier ist Halligalli“, sagt sie dann, „die Lautstärke nervt. Wenn man das eine Million Mal am Tag hat…“ Das nächste Auto, ein Porsche-Cayenne-Geländewagen, extralaut, sie unterbricht wieder."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d45c461-48ac-4595-a1ee-b6d4e15bc80e",
                                "sense_id": "7ae20b3d-e238-32d4-9a13-e2daf1b3cb68",
                                "text": "In der Wohnung ist Halligalli. So hat es seine Mutter immer genannt, wenn sie nach der Arbeit nach Hause kam und er vergessen hatte, vorher die Musik leisezudrehen. Was ist denn das für ein Halligalli, hatte sie dann gefragt und an allen Knöpfen gedreht."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "71dc4632-2120-4516-9a99-b8955cecbd03",
                        "source_entry_id": "4e5fcabd-a39b-385b-b934-e26bdca68327",
                        "source_sense_id": "669e468f-39ec-3ef8-8604-c0ca90db5efa",
                        "source_sense_description": "ausgelassenes Treiben",
                        "target_lang_word": "high jinks",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "high jinks",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "24d1f434-5792-31ef-8c42-7546b5cceea3",
                                        "entry_id": "21d2a8c5-edf0-3fc8-af76-2791b14df1d2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An old Scottish parlour game in which people were chosen, usually by throwing dice, to perform some humorous act or drink a large amount of an alcoholic beverage, with a forfeit if they were unable to do so."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Scotland",
                                            "historical",
                                            "plural",
                                            "plural-only"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32de344d-9033-485a-80e8-db05ac452b17",
                                                "sense_id": "24d1f434-5792-31ef-8c42-7546b5cceea3",
                                                "text": "[T]he frolicsome company had begun to practise the ancient and now forgotten pastime of High Jinks. This game was played in several different ways. Most frequently the dice were thrown by the company, and those upon whom the lot fell were obliged to assume and maintain, for a time, a certain fictitious character, or to repeat a certain number of fescennine verses in a particular order. If they departed from the characters assigned, or if their memory proved treacherous in the repetition, they incurred forfeits, which were either compounded for by swallowing an additional bumper, or by paying a small sum towards the reckoning."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "82e0d115-5f50-384b-bbfc-85575bfb44a7",
                                        "entry_id": "21d2a8c5-edf0-3fc8-af76-2791b14df1d2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Boisterous activity or behaviour; lively fun."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "plural",
                                            "plural-only"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0dc760fd-29ba-4de5-8e2d-d78f2caf8262",
                                                "sense_id": "82e0d115-5f50-384b-bbfc-85575bfb44a7",
                                                "text": "Only one tutor has rooms here; and I should think, if he's a reading man, it wont be for long before he clears out; for all sorts of high jinks go on on the grass-plot, and the row on the staircases is often as bad, and not half so respectable, as it used to be in the middle passage in the last week of the half year."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f24619d-15fe-41cf-90ba-f08c502ab168",
                                                "sense_id": "82e0d115-5f50-384b-bbfc-85575bfb44a7",
                                                "text": "But given the funny hats and juvenile hijinx, it's hard to buy the play's more serious intentions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc8eaaa7-b6c4-4919-82ba-db45c55fb3d5",
                                                "sense_id": "82e0d115-5f50-384b-bbfc-85575bfb44a7",
                                                "text": "Day of the Dead stretches the zombie film just about as far as it can go – and the film [George Andrew] Romero wanted to make could have been even more challenging – but the horror movie audience is more interested in the partying hi-jinx of trendy monsters like [Dan] O'Bannon's funky zombies, Freddy Krueger or Herbert West."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "71dae4c7-e042-31db-8924-1cbd54b6fd6c",
                                        "entry_id": "21d2a8c5-edf0-3fc8-af76-2791b14df1d2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tricky or waggish behaviour; mischief."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "plural",
                                            "plural-only"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d459af85-009b-4bf6-86f0-aebaa959105f",
                                                "sense_id": "71dae4c7-e042-31db-8924-1cbd54b6fd6c",
                                                "text": "High Jinks! High Jinks! High Jinks! The haggis has puttin' out the fire, and sealed up the boiler—"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36e165e5-42d4-4eae-a7a0-0429d6ccda59",
                                                "sense_id": "71dae4c7-e042-31db-8924-1cbd54b6fd6c",
                                                "text": "That's what happened to me the last time you fired a high snowball. Peaches. That's why I didn't want you to try another while I'm around. You wait until I'm off the campus if you've got to indulge in high jinks."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d030973-e40e-44ae-b75e-609e8cc59511",
                                                "sense_id": "71dae4c7-e042-31db-8924-1cbd54b6fd6c",
                                                "text": "It was a face familiar to millions of Americans around the country, an almost intimate face to anyone who'd ever watched a televised news program or any other national hi-jinks from Chicago."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e83a115-b107-4518-9abe-28f05114e9b8",
                                                "sense_id": "71dae4c7-e042-31db-8924-1cbd54b6fd6c",
                                                "text": "Those bastards hadn't left the school and gone back to their hi-jinks like we thought. Not at all. They'd been looking for us, eager to bash our brains in."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd472748-7f61-411c-8124-0d1ecd394e11",
                                                "sense_id": "71dae4c7-e042-31db-8924-1cbd54b6fd6c",
                                                "text": "Apparently the man had a reputation for hi[-]jinks, such as filing fake flight plans to deceive [Bill] Clinton's barnstorming rivals."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04be9f55-7e5c-42b8-91a6-b4fcb7eac08f",
                                                "sense_id": "71dae4c7-e042-31db-8924-1cbd54b6fd6c",
                                                "text": "Even though I have no arms or legs I did put my mom through some tough times. I did my share of rebellion and hi-jinx."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b636561-5fad-49ee-9f12-c9d8b2f38d3d",
                                                "sense_id": "71dae4c7-e042-31db-8924-1cbd54b6fd6c",
                                                "text": "You know those movies where the goofy housemate reads a book of spells on Halloween and hijinxs ensue?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53a14923-656a-4336-8fae-1a15cc2da3dc",
                                                "sense_id": "71dae4c7-e042-31db-8924-1cbd54b6fd6c",
                                                "text": "One could argue, of course, that most comedies about the risqué misadventures of teenagers are actually pretty wholesome. Horny hits like American Pie and last year's Blockers are, at heart, sweet coming-of-age stories, secretly reassuring everyone that the kids are all right—that no matter how many f-bombs they drop, no matter how raunchy their MPAA-antagonizing hijinks get, they're really just fumbling their inexperienced way through normal rites of passage."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
